.TH FGETS 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fgets \- read a line from a Crunch stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "char* fgets(char* " buffer ", int " size ", struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads at most
.I size
minus one bytes, stopping after a newline or end-of-file, and appends a NUL
byte. A newline that is read is retained. The buffer must have room for
.I size
bytes.
If
.I size
is one, an empty string is returned without reading from the stream.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns
.I buffer
on success. Returns null on end-of-file before any bytes are read, leaving the
buffer unchanged, or on a read error. On a read error the buffer's contents
are unspecified, the stream error indicator is set and
.B errno
is set.
A null buffer or stream or a nonpositive size fails with
.BR EINVAL ;
when the stream is valid its error indicator is set.
.SH NOTES
I/O is unbuffered. Only Crunch streams are supported; they are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fputs (3crunch),
.BR fgetc (3crunch),
.BR feof (3crunch),
.BR ferror (3crunch)
